# The Reading Is The Cache Boundary
#
# Why an apposition is the right granule for cache invalidation: it is
# author-declared, verifiable without a parse, perspectival by construction,
# and already placed 220 times across this corpus.
#
# @see .spw/biome/ocean/algos/cache.spw
# @see packages/spw-seed/src/lexer/matchers/apposition.ts
# @see packages/spw-seed/src/types/ast/nodes.ts (AppositionLabel)
# @see packages/spw-lsp/src/handlers/workspace.ts (volatilityOf)

#:layer #!pragmatics
#:cache #!granularity

^seed[Spw.Cache.AppositionGranule v:0.1 @profile:Spw.b @intent:granular_invalidation]

^["roots"]{
 @cache_spec: ~"../../../.spw/biome/ocean/algos/cache.spw"
 @apposition: ~"../../../packages/spw-seed/src/lexer/matchers/apposition.ts"
 @nodes: ~"../../../packages/spw-seed/src/types/ast/nodes.ts"
 @volatility: ~"../../../packages/spw-lsp/src/handlers/workspace.ts"
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Thesis
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

^["thesis"]{
 ~#value: "A cache needs granules. This language grew them for a different reason and has not noticed: an apposition marks a region and declares how to hold it, which is a boundary and a key in one mark."
 ~#status: "proposed"
 ~#premise: "Invalidation should be proportional to the edit. Today it is proportional to the file."
 ~#invariant: "A hit and a cold recompute return the same answer. Reuse is an optimization; correctness is not negotiable."
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Why this mark and not another
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

^["why_apposition"]{
 ~#declared: "The boundary is chosen by an author who knows what belongs together, not inferred from indentation or byte distance."

 ~#parse_free: .{
  fact: "the body is lexed raw to the matching paren"
  reason_given: "prose carries commas and apostrophes; tokenizing it would make ordinary phrasing a syntax error"
  consequence: "the whole apposition set of a surface is extractable by a scan"
  gift: "a validity probe at lexer cost for data that cost a parse — an ergonomic decision paying an unrelated debt"
 }

 ~#perspectival: "The parens are the @ container, so a reading is a declared perspective on a region. The language's perspective marker and the cache's view key are already the same object."

 ~#survives_edits: "A named apposition is an identity that outlives edits elsewhere in the file. Offsets are not. Line numbers are not. contentHash is not."

 ~#already_placed: .{
  neighbor: 157
  lens: 56
  name: 2
  anonymous: 5
  surfaces_covered: "182 of 493"
 }
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// What each key kind carries
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

^["key_kinds"]{
 ~#lens: "Declares the interpretation under which derived data was computed. Derived data keyed by lens invalidates when the lens changes, not when the file does — the selectorId of @cache_spec, supplied by the author instead of inferred."
 ~#neighbor: "Declares adjacency by hand. @cache_spec asks that coupled files share eviction fate and proposes deriving coupling from edges; 157 marks already assert it from someone who knows the corpus better than degree-counting does."
 ~#anonymous: "Anchors a span, supplies no key. Degrades to positional identity — the one identity that does not survive an edit. Five exist; they are the honest edge of this design."
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The envelope
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

^["envelope"]{
 ~#definition: "A granule's envelope is its apposition set plus the span hash of each — the cheap summary a scan can produce and a cache can compare."
 ~#decides: "reuse or reparse. Never correctness."
 ~#asymmetry: "A false 'changed' costs one reparse. A false 'unchanged' serves stale data. The probe must be conservative in exactly one direction."

 %[proportionality]: "An edit inside one granule leaves sibling envelopes unchanged. If that fails, the boundary is not stable and the premise is wrong."
 %[parity]: "The scan and the parser agree on every apposition in the corpus — same names, same bodies, same spans."
 %[fallback]: "63% of surfaces carry no apposition and fall back to whole-file invalidation. That path must not regress."
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// Standing on what already exists
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

^["inheritance"]{
 ~#from_spec: "@cache_spec already specifies composite keys, hash-prefix eviction, and coupling cascade. None are implemented. This plan treats the drift as the bug and the spec as the design."
 ~#from_volatility: "@volatility computes whether a surface's content keeps, on an axis independent of recency, and the evictor ignores it. Granularity is the first half; crossing tier with volatility is the second, deferred."
 ~#from_kernel: "ParseOutput already carries duration, lexProfile, and events — cost, key dimension, and instability signal. All three are dropped at the ServerIndex boundary."
}

^["open"]{
 ?[coverage]: "Does this pay for itself at 37% surface coverage? Measure reparse volume on a real edit sequence before building past the scan."
 ?[granule_identity]: "geometric-analysis-tooling will key on shapeFingerprint. One granule identity serving both, or two keyed views of one region?"
 ?[promotion]: "If the envelope probe holds, @cache_spec should absorb it as a named key kind rather than leaving it in a branch plan."
}
